## Part 4: CSS Styling

### 4.1 Main Styles (styles.css)

**Key Sections:**
- CSS Custom Properties (design tokens)
- Typography and base styles
- Component styles (buttons, cards, navbar)
- Layout utilities

### 4.2 Parallax Styles (parallax.css)

**Key Features:**
- Parallax container positioning
- Layer absolute positioning
- Transform origin settings for smooth movement
- Z-index layering system
- Hero content positioning

### 4.3 Responsive Styles (responsive.css)

**Breakpoints:**
- Mobile: 320px - 480px
- Tablet: 481px - 768px
- Desktop: 769px+

**Mobile Parallax Adjustments:**
- Reduced parallax movement intensity (40% of desktop)
- Simpler parallax on touch devices
- Optimized touch navigation
- Smaller images on mobile

---

## Part 5: JavaScript Implementation

### 5.1 Parallax Effect (parallax.js)

**Core Logic:**
// Mouse move event listener
// Track mouse position (x, y)
// Calculate offset based on mouse position
// Apply CSS transforms to parallax layers
// Use GSAP for smooth animations
// Handle throttling for performance

Key Functions:
- initParallax() - Initialize parallax elements
- onMouseMove(e) - Handle mouse tracking
- updateParallaxLayers(x, y) - Update layer positions
- resetParallax() - Reset on mouse leave

**Performance Optimization:**
- Throttle mousemove events (60fps)
- Use `transform: translate3d()` for GPU acceleration
- Avoid layout thrashing
- Use CSS `will-change` property strategically

### 5.2 Reveal Animation (reveal.js)

**Features:**
- Elements slide in from bottom on page load
- Staggered animation for visual flow
- Trigger on scroll using Intersection Observer API
- Smooth easing (ease-out-cubic)

**Implementation:**
// Intersection Observer for scroll triggers
// GSAP timeline for sequential animations
// Fade + translate from bottom effect
// 0.6-1.0s duration per element

### 5.3 Interactions (interactions.js)

**Features:**
- Hamburger menu toggle
- Smooth scroll navigation
- Navbar toggle on scroll
- Search functionality (optional)
- Keyboard navigation support

